{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>From above</b> — three times in the Masorah: ברכות שמים מעל. מטל השמים מעל. יקרא אל השמים מעל ואל הארץ לדין עמו. Meaning: for judgment of peoples He calls to the heavens to withhold dew and rain, and to the earth to withhold its produce, as written: כי בם ידין עמים." "<b>couches</b> — three times in the Masorah: here, and the others also in Joseph: ומתהום רובצת תחת. והאם רובצת. This is what we say in chapter 3 of Ta'anit: there is no drop that descends from above that does not have drops rising from below, from the deep — and that is ומתהום רובצת תחת. And והאם רובצת — derives רובצת רובצת from מתהום רובצת, to teach that one who finds a nest in the sea is obligated in sending her away." "<b>Blessings of the breasts</b> — these are the heavens that pour rain." "<b>and the womb</b> — this is the earth that gives birth to fruit."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:50.929277516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}